# Go
/bin/
*.test
*.out
# stray repo-root Go build artifacts from an ad-hoc `go build ./<pkg>` (real builds go to
# package.nix / a temp dir), named after their cmd dir.
/driver
/briard-agent
/witness-forwarder
/reverse-proxy-bin

# Nix
/result
/result-*
/.direnv/

# editor / OS
*.swp
.DS_Store

# secrets — never commit (loaded via direnv dotenv; see .envrc)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/.secrets/
/token
# Signing keys. The release key (RELEASE_SIGN_KEY, a PKCS8 PEM) belongs outside the tree
# entirely; this is a backstop against an unguarded `git add -A` committing the trust root of
# every node's updates, not the plan. [B.74]
*.pem

# The release staging directory `/publish-release` builds into: signed binaries, the guest
# qcow2, the qemu bundles. ~430 MB of build output that is republished from source every time,
# so it has no business in history — and in a PUBLIC repo it would be cloned by every user
# forever. Ignored for exactly the reason the key above is: an unguarded `git add -A` in a
# session that did not create it sweeps it in silently, which is how it got committed once
# already ([V3b.3](b), caught before any push). Stage named paths, not `-A`.
.release/
